  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Boundaries that hold",
      "items": [
        "Every /vault/ page and every approval needs an Access JWT for the garden's own application (CF_GARDEN_AUD); only Cloudflare signs it",
        "Lettuce's JWT, which reaches the BFF in plain HTTP, is for another audience: the vault refuses it, and check_garden_audience refuses a stack where it would not",
        "Pages load only as top-level documents and forms post only from the garden origin (Fetch Metadata); every response sets COOP same-origin",
        "/mcp and /redeem answer only Host garden-vault with no Origin; the tunnel routes only /vault/ to the vault",
        "The data key lives only in the vault process while unlocked; a lock drops handles and uncollected values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not a boundary",
      "items": [
        "BFF and app-server share one network namespace; agents run as root in the app-server",
        "Agents can call /mcp and /redeem themselves, so approval is the gate",
        "vault-run keeps values out of the conversation, but an agent could redeem a handle directly"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown",
      "items": [
        "Other garden pages on the same host (gmail-triggers, the code editor) and Lettuce's opt-in services",
        "The LLM provider that the app-server calls",
        "lettucectl on the host: builds and checks each stack, registers the vault in Settings -> MCP (lettucectl mcp), installs vault-run (lettucectl skills)"
      ]
    }
  ]
